# HTTP requests for the External Key Custodian sample.
#
# Run these inline from VS Code (with the REST Client extension) or a JetBrains IDE, or import them into
# Postman, Bruno, or Hoppscotch. Trust the dev HTTPS certificate once so the client accepts it:
#     dotnet dev-certs https --trust

@host = https://localhost:5001

### Fetch an access token (OAuth 2.0 client_credentials). It is signed inside the custodian.
# @name token
POST {{host}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=demo-service&client_secret=secret&scope=api

### The published keys: public-only (kty, n, e), never any private material.
GET {{host}}/.well-known/jwks

### Introspect the token. With Provider:EncryptAccessToken on, this makes the server unwrap the
### Content Encryption Key through the custodian before it can validate the token.
POST {{host}}/connect/introspect
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

token={{token.response.body.$.access_token}}&client_id=demo-service&client_secret=secret
